<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ion of Chios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 490–c. 420 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ion of Chios was a Greek poet and prose writer of the fifth century BCE who spent much of his life in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>. He wrote tragedies, lyric poetry and a work of reminiscences describing meetings with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sophocles">Sophocles</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pericles">Pericles</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cimon">Cimon</a>, one of the earliest examples of memoir in Greek. He also recorded the island's foundation legends in a history of Chios.</p></div>
